dhp164:1 starts: The teaching of those who live the Dhamma,
dhp164:2 starts: worthy ones, noble:
dhp164:3 starts: whoever maligns it
dhp164:4 starts: –a dullard,
dhp164:5 starts: bears fruit for his own destruction,
dhp164:6 starts: like the fruiting of the bamboo.
iti62:4.1 starts: then, from the ending
iti62:4.2 starts: there’s the knowledge,
iti62:4.3 starts: the gnosis of one released
iti62:4.4 starts: ‘My release is unprovoked.’
snp2.6:5.1 starts: Arriving at deprivation,
snp2.6:5.2 starts: from womb to womb,
snp2.6:5.3 starts: a monk of this sort, after death,
snp2.6:5.4 starts: comes to suffering.
snp2.6:6.1 starts: Just like a cesspit, full, used for many
snp2.6:6.2 starts: one of this sort, befouled,
snp2.6:6.3 starts: would be hard to clean.
snp2.6:6.4 none
snp2.6:8.1 starts: all of you, united, shun him.
snp2.6:8.2 starts: Sweep away the sweepings,
snp2.6:8.3 starts: throw away the trash,
snp2.6:8.4 none
